-- dynamic colors: a string variable names the color; a string that shadows a
-- palette name wins; an unknown string falls back to white; a non-string variable
-- does not shadow a literal palette word
shade is green
shadow is dark gray
red is blue
weird is "not-a-color"
score is 4
yellow is 4
clear screen to shade
draw rect at 2, 2 size 4, 4 in shadow
draw circle at 20, 20 size 5 in red
draw rect at 50, 2 size 4, 4 in yellow
pset 40, 40 in shade
write "hi {shade}" at 2, 20 in weird
show meter score of 10 at 2, 40 in shade
burst 4 sparks at 60, 60 in shadow
